PM: G2(a) complete (box art-g2-bake/OUT/REPORT.md; code feature/art-g2, unmerged, new files only). Re-baked normal/basecolor/RM at 2k from the 947-972k high-poly onto each retopo (Cycles selected-to-active, cage 0.015*max dim, 16px EXTEND), applied to rigged FBX via shared UVs (max UV delta 0 for all four; mouse has the known 0.0039 Y offset). Fixture check at native 105/66/47/190 + 4x: badger/fox/mouse show no clear useful detail gain (only subtle shading); boar shows visible but mixed fur/shoulder/coat changes, not uniformly better. Normal maps are sharper in the atlas but have saturated UV-border wedges and flatter/faceted basecolor patches (due to fragmented Tripo UV packing). The first basecolor bake darkened metals (diffuse pass attenuated by metallic): fixed in the second attempt via emit-transfer of raw Base Color. 4k vs 2k (badger, boar): no visible gain at game size -> 2k is sufficient, stopping at 2k. No green-channel inversion. RM: G=roughness, B=metallic, unjudged because the fixture forces metallic 0 / smoothness 0.25. My assessment: re-baking from the high-poly is not worth adopting as is; the 1k->2k detail gap is not what limits the look at 105 px. Maps are in ~/Desktop/tripo-g0/baked/<name>/ if you want them. Proposal: skip adoption, move to G2(b) cast style consistency via materials only (one shader, per-class metallic/smoothness ranges for cloth/leather/metal/fur, shared grading). Note: the fixture currently forces metallic 0 / smoothness 0.25 on every actor, so (b) needs a fixture variant that allows class ranges through and a class map per character (material slots or a mask). Shall I dispatch (b) as designed, or do you want it scoped differently? Owner has not yet answered the G1 look judgement.
